@0    = ~Oops - you dropped something from your pack, <CHARNAME> - let me just pick it up for you. There. Now, I'll just get back in line.~
@1    = ~I can't believe you are so blatant. Did she not see you staring at...um, staring at her?~
@2    = ~Me? Stare? I'd never do such a thing. Well, maybe a little, but...~
@3    = ~Wait, you're actually annoyed, aren't you? What's got your hair in a knot?~
@4    = ~I'm just confused about why you think pulling such a cheap trick would get you anywhere.~
@5    = ~Must be uncomfortable living in a world where everything's got to mean something. Maybe I was just being nice. Or am I not allowed to do that?~
@6    = ~It's strange to think how far we've come, just in this short time of knowing one another, isn't it? I'd like to think that--~
@7    = ~Kelsey, some friendly advice. You want to get a girl, don't spout philosophy at her at every turn. Better still, leave off the sob stories.~
@8    = ~Funny. If it makes you feel big to make jokes at me, go right ahead, but would you mind not listening in when I'm having a private conversation with a friend?~
@9    = ~Oh, I get it. Are you jealous, now? Just because I'm getting to know <CHARNAME> and you're not?~
@10   = ~If by 'jealous' you mean 'wishing I didn't have to listen to you going on about your bad situation', then yeah, I am.~
@11   = ~Not all men are like you - sometimes they actually enjoy getting to know a woman rather than jumping on them as soon as they get the chance.~
@12   = ~Don't come all high and mighty with me. Like you haven't got that on your mind!~
@13   = ~You know how you're coming across? You've had your fill of dancing girls, or whatever, and now you want to try your hand with <CHARNAME>, just because you can.~
@14   = ~Maybe <CHARNAME> should say whether she likes me trying my hand with her, yeah?~
@15   = ~I don't like to make a choice, but I prefer Kelsey over you, Faren.~
@16   = ~You can't give me what I want. Kelsey's the man for me.~
@17   = ~I enjoy Kelsey's company, but I prefer you.~
@18   = ~As if I'd take up with that accountant! You're a lot more fun.~
@19   = ~Enough of this, both of you! I just want to be friends with you both.~
@20   = ~Oh. Okay. I guess that's that, then.~
@21   = ~Thank you, <CHARNAME>. I'm glad we could get this sorted out.~
@22   = ~Well...well, anyway, I didn't think this was going anywhere.~
@23   = ~Good to know where we stand, <CHARNAME>.~
@24   = ~I don't think I'm ever going to get used to people trying to push me around. Just when I think it'll stop happening, some Shadowmaster or demon or Cowled bureaucrat decides it'll be fun to use me as some sort of plaything.~
@25   = ~I'd call that normal - happens to us all. Mostly, I just let them think they've got the upper hand. If they underestimate you, they'll leave you in peace.~
@26   = ~To be honest, I think underestimation's the problem.~
@27   = ~Ah, I see. You could always get an earring, or grow your hair, or something. Make yourself look a bit more menacing.~
@28   = ~That...isn't really what I had in mind, but thank you, I guess.~
@29   = ~Wear taller shoes?~
@30   = ~(sigh)~
@31   = ~For the last time, Faren, no, you cannot have a 'Coltrane discount' next time you're buying...what was it again? 'Exotic Tribeswomen of the Northern Realms'?~
@32   = ~Yeah, that's the one. C'mon, can't you--~
@33   = ~I don't think we even stocked that kind of thing, anyway. At least I hope not.~
@34   = ~Damn, now you've got everyone looking at us. I mean, no! Kelsey, why would I want to buy such, um, such sordid material?~
@35   = ~Your eye twitches when you know no one will believe you.~
@36   = ~There we go, foiled again!~
@37   = ~Godsdammit, but my feet are aching.~
@38   = ~We're all tired and hungry. Maybe if you didn't go on about it so much, you wouldn't be in so much pain.~
@39   = ~Wasn't doing it to bother you. You have a problem with it, you tell it to my face.~
@40   = ~I thought I just did. I'm fed up of hearing you make a fuss when other people have it worse off than you.~
@41   = ~I mean, Aerie's gone through so much, and you don't hear her complaining.~
@42   = ~Much.~
@43   = ~Look, I'm just dealing with it my own way. If it doesn't suit you, well, that's your problem.~
